  "runs_for_half_between_sd": null,
  "caveats": [
    "The world is held at LAW_R0 for the whole run (regime_cycles = cycles), because the readout is formed under that law and a rotation inside the scored window would change the generating process partway through a run. The frozen design's default world rotates at REGIME_SWITCH_CYCLE; the ladder's 1x cell is therefore not the frozen world's 150-200 window.",
    "The intervention is the scored window at fixed exposure (110 formation cycles). A longer exposure is a different intervention and is not measured.",
    "The between-run SD rests on five worlds. It is an estimate of that spread, not its population value, and rho inherits its error.",
    "The endpoint is one comparator family, chosen by tuning loss as in the frozen studies. A different baseline family would move the delta, and the decomposition is about this contrast.",
    "Within-run variability is measured by resampling contiguous quarters of one world; it measures sampling error inside a run, not how a different world would have differed."
  ],
